Boundary Fill Algorithm
1. Boundary Fill Algorithm starts at a pixel inside the polygon to be filled and paints the
interior proceeding outwards towards the boundary.
2. This algorithm works only if the color with which the region has to be filled and the color of
the boundary of the region are different. If the boundary is of one single color, this approach
proceeds outwards pixel by pixel until it hits the boundary of the region.
3. Boundary Fill Algorithm is recursive in nature. It takes an interior point(x, y), a fill color,
and a boundary color as the input. The algorithm starts by checking the color of (x, y).
4. If it's color is not equal to the fill color and the boundary color, then it is painted with the fill
color and the function is called for all the neighbours of (x, y).
5. If a point is found to be of fill color or of boundary color, the function does not call its
neighbours and returns.
6. This process continues until all points up to the boundary color for the region have been
tested.

How Does the Boundary Fill Algorithm Work?
The boundary fill algorithm operates by checking the color of each neighbouring pixel. If the color
of the pixel matches the target color, it gets filled with a new color, and the algorithm proceeds to its
neighbours. The process continues until all the pixels inside the boundary are filled.
